.SH NAME
md_CONTRIBUTING \- 🤝 SystemEx Contributing 
.PP


.PP
Thank you for your interest in contributing to \fBSystemEx\fP\&. 
.br
 This document explains how to report issues, propose improvements, and submit pull requests\&.
.SH "How to Contribute"
.PP
.SS "1\&. Reporting Issues"
When opening an issue, please include:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
A clear description of the problem 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Reproduction steps (if applicable) 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Expected vs\&. actual behavior 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Relevant code snippets or logs 
.br

.PP

.PP
Clear reports help maintainers understand and address issues efficiently\&.
.SS "2\&. Proposing Changes"
Before submitting large changes or refactors, please open a discussion or issue\&. 
.br
 \fBSystemEx\fP is highly modular and low‑level; major changes can introduce subtle regressions\&.

.PP
Small patches, documentation improvements, and targeted fixes are always welcome\&.
.SS "3\&. Pull Requests"
Pull requests should:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Be focused and minimal 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Include a description of the change 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Avoid unnecessary formatting changes 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Respect existing architecture and module boundaries 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Not introduce deep cross‑dependencies between subsystems 
.br

.PP
.SH "Architectural Notes"
.PP
\fBSystemEx\fP intentionally avoids tight coupling between modules\&. 
.br
 Some structures exist in multiple forms (e\&.g\&., \fRMap<TKey, TValue>\fP based on \fRPair<TKey, TValue>[]\fP) to keep subsystems isolated and easier to debug\&.

.PP
This is a deliberate design choice\&.
.SH "Experimental Features and Development Flags"
.PP
\fBSystemEx\fP contains optional experimental code guarded by the build flag \fRUSE_DEVBUILD_UNSTABLE\fP\&. These sections include work‑in‑progress modules, unstable APIs, debugging utilities, or partially implemented subsystems\&. They are intentionally excluded from normal builds to keep the repository stable and free from unfinished code paths\&.

.PP
If you want to contribute to experimental areas, you must explicitly enable the flag in your build configuration:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
For MSBuild: add \fR<DefineConstants>USE_DEVBUILD_UNSTABLE</DefineConstants>\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
For command‑line builds: pass \fR/p:DefineConstants=USE_DEVBUILD_UNSTABLE\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
For IDE builds: add the symbol to your project’s build settings
.PP

.PP
When contributing to experimental code:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Expect incomplete or placeholder implementations 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Expect rapid changes and refactors 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Do not rely on experimental APIs for production code 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Keep experimental contributions isolated and well‑scoped 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
Avoid introducing dependencies from stable modules into unstable ones 
.br

.PP

.PP
Experimental features may be removed, rewritten, or replaced without notice\&. They exist solely to support active development and prototyping\&.
.SH "🕒 Response Times"
.PP
\fBSystemEx\fP is maintained by a single author (pronouns: dey/deren/dem/dem)\&. 
.br
 Responses or reviews may occasionally be delayed, but all constructive contributions are appreciated\&.

.PP
Thank you for helping improve \fBSystemEx\fP\&. 
